course: dictionary
lesson: 11205
title: Wolof: a people, a language, a word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Wolof is the name of a people of West Africa, and also the name of their language. Most Wolof people live in Senegal, The Gambia and Mauritania. «In Senegal many people speak French and Wolof» tells you that Wolof is a language people use every day, next to French.
explain: The words around Wolof show you which meaning fits. In «Wolof music», Wolof describes the music, so it is an adjective: the music belongs to the Wolof people or their language. The capital W shows that it is a name.
explain: Not everyone who speaks Wolof is Wolof. The dictionary says it is widely spoken in Senegal, including by people who are not Wolof. When you read a word, ask: is it naming a people, naming a language, or describing something?
fact: Wolof is a people of West Africa, and also the name of their language.
fact: Most Wolof people live in Senegal, The Gambia and Mauritania.
fact: Wolof is written with a capital W because it is a name.
fact: As an adjective, «Wolof» describes things of the Wolof people or language, such as «Wolof music».
fact: Experts are not sure whether English words like «banana» and «jive» come from Wolof.
exercise: In «many people speak French and Wolof», what is Wolof? | A type of fruit | A country | *A language | A kind of music
exercise: In «Wolof music», what kind of word is Wolof? | A question word | A verb | *An adjective | A country
exercise: Which country is NOT a place where most Wolof people live? | Senegal | *Brazil | Mauritania | The Gambia
test: The penpal in «one in Dakar mixes French and Wolof» lives in which city? | *Dakar | Montreal | Brussels | Paris
test: Which statement is true? | Only Wolof people speak Wolof | Wolof is a kind of French cheese | *Many people who are not Wolof speak Wolof, especially in Senegal | Wolof is a town in Montreal
exam: Which penpal in the text says «septante» for 70? | *Brussels | Paris | Dakar | Montreal
